=       import construables.pngConstruable
-       ```
+       ```

-       Nothing is construed without a deliberate choice: `import soundness.*` brings none of
-       these in, and each is imported by name. The package merges with the umbrella's own
-       `construables`, so the import is the same whichever library the given came from.
-   entry .pngConstruable   `image/png` construes as a `Raster in Png`
-       In `hallucination.png`. Import it by name: `import construables.pngConstruable`.
-   entry .gifConstruable   `image/gif` construes as a `Raster in Gif`
-       In `hallucination.gif`. Import it by name: `import construables.gifConstruable`.
-   entry .bmpConstruable   `image/bmp` construes as a `Raster in Bmp`
-       In `hallucination.bmp`. Import it by name: `import construables.bmpConstruable`.
+       Nulla viene interpretato senza una scelta deliberata: `import soundness.*` non porta
+       nessuno di questi, e ciascuno si importa per nome. Il package si fonde con il
+       `construables` proprio del modulo ombrello, così l'import è lo stesso qualunque sia la
+       libreria da cui proviene il given.
+   entry .pngConstruable   `image/png` si interpreta come `Raster in Png`
+       In `hallucination.png`. Va importato per nome: `import construables.pngConstruable`.
+   entry .gifConstruable   `image/gif` si interpreta come `Raster in Gif`
+       In `hallucination.gif`. Va importato per nome: `import construables.gifConstruable`.
+   entry .bmpConstruable   `image/bmp` si interpreta come `Raster in Bmp`
+       In `hallucination.bmp`. Va importato per nome: `import construables.bmpConstruable`.

-   entry .jpegConstruable   construes an `image/jpeg` response as a `Raster in Jpeg`
-       The given `("image/jpeg" is Construable to (Raster in Jpeg))`, declared in
-       `hallucination.jpeg`, which tells a media-typed client (such as an apoplexy `Api`) that a
-       body of media type `image/jpeg` is read as a `Raster in Jpeg`, through `Jpeg`'s own codec.
-       The typeclass carries no operations of its own. It lives in the `construables` choice
-       package and so must be imported by name, `import construables.jpegConstruable`; `import
-       soundness.*` does not bring it in.
-   entry .webpConstruable   construes an `image/webp` response as a `Raster in Webp`
-       The given `("image/webp" is Construable to (Raster in Webp))`, declared in
-       `hallucination.webp`, which tells a media-typed client (such as an apoplexy `Api`) that a
-       body of media type `image/webp` is read as a `Raster in Webp`, through `Webp`'s own codec.
-       It lives in the `construables` choice package and so must be imported by name, `import
-       construables.webpConstruable`; `import soundness.*` does not bring it in.
+   entry .jpegConstruable   interpreta una risposta `image/jpeg` come `Raster in Jpeg`
+       Il given `("image/jpeg" is Construable to (Raster in Jpeg))`, dichiarato in
+       `hallucination.jpeg`, che dice a un client tipizzato per tipo di media (come un `Api` di
+       apoplexy) che un corpo di tipo di media `image/jpeg` si legge come `Raster in Jpeg`,
+       attraverso il codec proprio di `Jpeg`. La typeclass non porta operazioni proprie. Vive nel
+       package di scelta `construables` e quindi va importato per nome, `import
+       construables.jpegConstruable`; `import soundness.*` non lo porta.
+   entry .webpConstruable   interpreta una risposta `image/webp` come `Raster in Webp`
+       Il given `("image/webp" is Construable to (Raster in Webp))`, dichiarato in
+       `hallucination.webp`, che dice a un client tipizzato per tipo di media (come un `Api` di
+       apoplexy) che un corpo di tipo di media `image/webp` si legge come `Raster in Webp`,
+       attraverso il codec proprio di `Webp`. Vive nel package di scelta `construables` e quindi
+       va importato per nome, `import construables.webpConstruable`; `import soundness.*` non lo
+       porta.

- entry .Jpeg   the JPEG format: `Raster in Jpeg`, read and written by a baseline and progressive DCT codec
+ entry .Jpeg   il formato JPEG: `Raster in Jpeg`, letto e scritto da un codec DCT baseline e progressivo

= entry .Jpeg   the JPEG format: `Raster in Jpeg`, read and written by a baseline and progressive DCT codec
-   detail
+   detail

-       `Jpeg` is the phantom format type of a JPEG raster, `Raster in Jpeg`, and its companion
-       holds the codec as the given `.rasterization`, a `Jpeg is Rasterizable`, which is in
-       implicit scope wherever `Jpeg` is named. `Jpeg()` returns that same instance as a plain
-       `Rasterizable` value, for `Raster.Formats(Jpeg(), …)` and for `Raster.Error(Jpeg())`.
-       The type is a sealed trait with no instances: it exists only to be written in a type.
+       `Jpeg` è il tipo di formato fantasma di un raster JPEG, `Raster in Jpeg`, e il suo
+       oggetto compagno contiene il codec come given `.rasterization`, un `Jpeg is
+       Rasterizable`, che è nell'ambito implicito ovunque `Jpeg` sia nominato. `Jpeg()`
+       restituisce quella stessa istanza come semplice valore `Rasterizable`, per
+       `Raster.Formats(Jpeg(), …)` e per `Raster.Error(Jpeg())`. Il tipo è un sealed trait
+       senza istanze: esiste solo per essere scritto in un tipo.

